  "groundingSupports": [
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 131,
        "endIndex": 227,
        "text": "#### **[0] Claude Opus 5.5 (anthropic.com)**\n* **Confirmed:** Anthropic launched Claude Opus 5.5"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 229,
        "endIndex": 402,
        "text": "The new model matches the performance of flagship model Fable 5.1 across most benchmarks while reducing running costs by roughly 20–40% ($4/1M input, $20/1M output tokens)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 404,
        "endIndex": 501,
        "text": "Anthropic highlighted enhanced safety alignment and safeguards against autonomous risky behaviour"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 592,
        "endIndex": 752,
        "text": "#### **[1] GPT-6 Sol and Luna (openai.com)**\n* **Confirmed:** OpenAI released two new lightweight models within its GPT-6 family, named GPT-6 Sol and GPT-6 Luna"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 754,
        "endIndex": 851,
        "text": "The models offer lower-latency, lower-cost inference designed for high-volume developer workloads"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 853,
        "endIndex": 932,
        "text": "* **Caveats:** The launch occurred within hours of Anthropic's Opus 5.5 release"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2501,
        "endIndex": 2950,
        "text": "#### **[5] Six major banks warn that increased autonomy for agentic commerce chatbots could lead to more scams, fraud, and disputes (Gizmodo)**\n* **Confirmed:** A joint industry report co-authored by six global banks (including Bank of America and Capital One) warns that autonomous \"agentic commerce\" shopping bots pose severe risks regarding financial scams, unauthorized transactions, data privacy, and dispute resolution as AI autonomy increases"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3,
        4,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3168,
        "endIndex": 3507,
        "text": "#### **[6] Pentagon says overreliance on AI contributed to missile strike on Iran school (Bloomberg)**\n* **Confirmed:** A Bloomberg report on an internal Pentagon investigation revealed that a February 28 US missile strike on Shajarah Tayyebeh Elementary School in Minab, Iran (killing over 120 children), was caused by a cascade of errors"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6,
        7,
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3509,
        "endIndex": 3699,
        "text": "These included heavy reliance on Palantir’s Maven AI targeting software, outdated satellite imagery, unlinked intelligence tools, and severe staffing cuts to civilian harm mitigation units"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6,
        7,
        8,
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3701,
        "endIndex": 3793,
        "text": "* **Caveats:** Findings are based on unreleased Pentagon probe details obtained by Bloomberg"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        7,
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3795,
        "endIndex": 3892,
        "text": "Palantir stated its software was not responsible for underlying data or intelligence deficiencies"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4007,
        "endIndex": 4282,
        "text": "#### **[7] OpenAI GPT-6 Astra breaks Enigma message that has resisted solution since 2005 (cryptocellar.org)**\n* **Confirmed:** Carter Leffen (a Bloomberg developer) used OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra to solve an unbroken 1941 German Army 82-letter Enigma ciphertext (indicator MVUEH)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10,
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4284,
        "endIndex": 4379,
        "text": "The break was independently verified by Enigma historian and CryptoCellar curator Frode Weierud"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10,
        12
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4381,
        "endIndex": 4667,
        "text": "* **Caveats:** The solution was achieved using a human-provided contextual clue (a guessed location, \"ROSENOW\", from a related message sent the same day) to construct a custom Enigma simulator script and search space rather than a pure mathematical codebreak of the Enigma cipher itself"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        13,
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 4737,
        "endIndex": 5090,
        "text": "#### **[8] Go.AI raised an $85M Series A led by Updata Partners (Axios)**\n* **Confirmed:** Go.AI (formerly Go Abacus), a Chicago-based startup building on-premises, examiner-ready AI hardware and software appliances for banks and regulated sectors, announced an $85M Series A round led by Updata Partners, with participation from GFT Ventures and LAUNCH"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        14,
        15
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
